		{"id":"720a5c2290a47bcb","type":"text","text":"- Declare new list of dictionaries where the key is an int tuple and the value is a char\n- Initialize current row index as zero\n- Initialize current column index as zero\n- Initialize is going down as true\n- Traverse string\n\t- Create a new dictionary entry:\n\t\t- Current row and column are the key and the current letter is the value\n\t- If going down\n\t\t- Increase current row index\n\t\t- If current row index > number of rows - 1\n\t\t\t- Current row = current row - 2\n\t\t\t- If Current row > 0\n\t\t\t\t- Is going down = false\n\t\t\t- Current column++\n\t- Else\n\t\t- Current row--\n\t\t- Current column++\n\t\t- If current row = 0\n\t\t\t- Is going down = true\n\t\t\t  \n- Let result = empty string\n- For row = 0, row < numrows, i++\n\t- For col = 0, col <= currentColIndex; col++\n\t\t- If value exists in dictionary for tuple\n\t\t\t- Add to result\n- Return result","x":-300,"y":460,"width":660,"height":720},
